  vfs:
    owner: os.kernel.fs
    lane: A03
    maturity: partial
    note: VfsHandleTable handle->mount routing landed (8 mounts[0] bypasses removed in services/vfs + LLM dispatch); src/lib fs_driver + 4 FAT32 copies still coexist — full collapse multi-increment; FAT32 copies 4->3, deleted src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/fs_driver/fat32_{core,dir_ops,hardening,parsers,stub,test_device}.spl (3165 lines, shadowed dead code: std.fs_driver.* resolves nogc_async_mut first, zero explicit importers; proven by async-only-symbol probe + failing sync-path control). FAT32B increment: sync fs_driver tier collapsed to shims — deleted ramfs/mount_table/direct_io/extension/driver_adapter/instance/ops (2477 lines, same shadowing, 15-vs-15 lockstep commit history, zero explicit importers) + orphaned fat32_cache.spl and its 2 spec copies (1017 lines; VFS2 delete-condition resolved: async fat32_core has 0 Dict refs / 77 flat-cache-field refs, never adopted it, and doc/09_report/nogc_eviction_leak_audit_2026-07-25.md confirms a leak in its 4 classes). −3494 net; 25 stale @cover paths repointed to async + 1 VFS2 dangling read_file guard repaired; all spec block counts byte-identical to baseline, Stage-S duplicate_owner guard 7 ✓/0 ✗, resolve probe PASS on JIT and interpreter. FAT32C increment: retired legacy driver deleted — src/os/services/fat32/{fat32,fat32_write,fat32_filesystem_ops,fat32_write_helpers}.spl (2122 lines) plus its 2 orphaned fat32_spec.spl copies (106 lines); island re-verified independently (zero src/ importers, imported only by each other, shared_fat32_driver delegates to std.fs_driver.fat32_core, no boot path / image builder / .shs reference). vfs_pure_fat_production_guard_spec.spl guard block was NOT removed but STRENGTHENED from non-use to absence: _assert_legacy_fat_implementation_files_deleted() asserts the 4 paths never reappear under src/os, and the tree walk lost its 4-file exemption so it now covers all of src/os; negative control confirmed the new assertion fails when the files are present (JIT + interpreter). −2232 net (git diff --stat: 22 insertions / 2254 deletions). All 15 vfs/arch/fs_driver spec block counts byte-identical to baseline; Stage-S duplicate_owner guard 7 ✓/0 ✗ on JIT and interpreter. FAT32 copies 3->2 — remaining: src/os/kernel/fs/fat32.spl (813, blocked on a target_presets.spl allowed_families decision, boot-path change needing QEMU+board validation); plan in .spipe/fs_stack_collapse/state.md §6 and .spipe/fat32_island_deletion/state.md
