    owner: os.posix
    lane: A05
    maturity: partial
    note: writable shared mmap now has a kernel MODEL (vmm_shared.spl shared page-cache objects + rights attenuation + msync/last-unmap write-back + frame-residency refcount separate from the map refcount, which closes a mapped-but-unfaulted use-after-free on the shared frame; spec 9 blocks/45 examples/0 failures on JIT and interpreter, incl. a deliberate-red calibration block); physical-frame path unproven on hardware (needs OVMF QEMU two-task gate), libc mmap still fails closed EOPNOTSUPP, syscall/VFS wiring not landed, SQLite WAL still blocked; no pthreads
  tty:
    owner: os.kernel tty paths
    lane: A06
    maturity: partial
    note: tty_write now delivers bytes to a drainable output buffer; PTY master/slave round-trip pending
  ssh:
    owner: os simple-native sshd
    lane: A06
    maturity: model
    note: maturity=model UNDERSTATES this - recommend partial. OpenSSH port RETRACTED as the production path - pure-Simple server src/os/apps/sshd (9576 lines) implements transport+curve25519 KEX+strict-kex+ext-info, ed25519/rsa-sha2-256,512/ecdsa-p256 host keys, aes256/128-gcm + aes256-ctr-etm (note: the LIVE server path ssh_cipher_live.spl is C-accelerated via tls13_aes256_gcm_helper.c; the pure-Simple ssh_cipher.spl is what the client uses), hmac-sha2-etm, channels/pty/exec, and interops with a real OpenSSH client in the x64 QEMU gate; pure-Simple client src/os/tools/net/_SshTool (1045 lines) reuses that core. rt_ssh_* SFFI (ssh_sffi/ssh_ffi) is a dead facade - NOP/weak-nil stubs only, no libssh2 anywhere. GAPS: ssh_kex.spl does not re-export ssh_sign_exchange_hash so ssh_kex_hostkey_matrix_spec is 1/7 (6x 'function not found', its rsa/ecdsa/kexinit describes never run) ssh_kex_rsa_contract_spec is 0/1 AND sshd_production_packet_transcript_spec (the full end-to-end version/KEX/NEWKEYS/auth/channel walk) is 0/1 - the host-key signing matrix and the only in-process full-session test are UNVERIFIED at HEAD on BOTH engines (one-line export fix); host-key algorithm advertisement IGNORES daemon policy - sshd_production_session_kexinit_spec 0/2, the daemon still advertises ssh-ed25519 when config disables it and configured RSA cert material never reaches the advertised list (real assertion failures, not resolution errors); interactive shell bridge RED at HEAD (ssh_session_shell_spec 5/7 - both echo round-trips return banner+prompt only, command never runs; the 5 greens are exec/SMF resolution not interactive execution); publickey userauth signature verify DISABLED (ssh_auth.spl:354), plaintext password store, no server-initiated rekey threshold (client-initiated rekey works), no subsystem/sftp, no port-forward, no chacha20-poly1305, client not wired to guest shell (register_tools.spl:91 stub) and blocked on guest rt_io_tcp_connect being a NOP. SPEC EVIDENCE 2026-07-28 (20 ssh specs, 124 examples, 94 pass / 30 fail, 13 green / 7 red; JIT and --mode=interpreter byte-identical so no engine artifacts, and 14 of the 30 failures are the single missing export above): GREEN = packet protocol + malformed-input hardening (27 ex), KEXINIT build/parse/negotiate + RFC4253 layout (24), constant-time password auth + MAC verify (26), PEM/DER host-key load (8). UNPROVEN = host-key SIGNING for every algorithm, the full-session transcript, and Ed25519 verify. Crypto KATs: curve25519 9/10 (sole red is an internal BigInt backend probe, not an RFC vector - all RFC 7748 TV1/TV2 + both ECDH directions pass), chacha20-poly1305 12/12, aes256-gcm 12/12, hmac 12/12, hkdf 9/9, rsa-pkcs1 10/10, sha2 2/8 (both reds are missing sha256_hex/sha512_hex exports, the byte-level multi-block digests pass); ed25519 SIGN byte-exact vs RFC 8032 but VERIFY aborts the runner in the std copy and the os.crypto copy's only spec reports 'no examples executed' - the client lane below identifies the cause as os.crypto.ed25519 not being JIT-lowerable ('Unknown type: u128'). Only 17% of the 9576 server lines (5 of 27 files) carry an @cover target - the session state machine is backed solely by the QEMU live gate. Bounded day-scale work, not multi-week. CLIENT LANE 2026-07-28: new pure-Simple client tree src/os/apps/ssh_client (7 modules, ~1500 lines) implements the direction-ASYMMETRIC half only and REUSES sshd ssh_packet/ssh_transport(parse+negotiate)/ssh_kex_core verbatim - no second packet or KEX implementation. Adds what was missing: known_hosts host-key PINNING (absent from _SshTool entirely - it only checked that the signature matched the key the server just sent, worthless vs MITM) with fail-closed verify (Ok(true) reachable only on exact host+algo+blob match; unknown -> refuse, changed -> distinct HOST KEY MISMATCH refuse; pin checked BEFORE signature verify and before any key derivation), pure-Simple ed25519 host-key signature verification replacing _SshTool's SFFI std.io.signature_sffi.verify_host_key (rt_ed25519_verify - C, cannot run in-guest), publickey/ed25519 userauth request signing with session-id binding, and a socket-free client state machine. 45 spec examples across 4 files, 0 failures (A/B CAVEAT: all 4 specs transitively import os.crypto.ed25519, which cannot be JIT-lowered at HEAD - 'HIR lowering error: Unknown type: u128' - so the default lane and SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE=interpreter run the SAME engine; a real JIT A/B of the SSH client is impossible until that u128 gap closes, and this is also why each ed25519 op costs ~3s); in-process client<->sshd handshake PROVEN (client KEX_ECDH_INIT parsed by real ssh_parse_kex_ecdh_init; real ssh_build_kex_ecdh_reply/ssh_build_kexinit/ssh_build_newkeys/ssh_build_service_accept/ssh_build_auth_success drive the client through exec + exit status; real curve25519 + ed25519, no mocks). 2 deliberate-red calibrations applied alone and reverted green. NOT DONE: record layer (AES-GCM framing) not attached, no socket wiring, no live gate, ed25519 host keys only, PTY/rekey/sftp absent - the client is spec-proven at the payload layer, NOT live-proven. DUPLICATION TO RESOLVE: two client trees now exist - _SshTool should keep its socket I/O and delegate protocol logic to os.apps.ssh_client (next-increment #1). Survey: .spipe/ssh_native_survey/state.md Client lane: .spipe/ssh_native_client/state.md
  tls:
    owner: os.tls13 (+ os.tls12 scaffolding, src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/tls for 1.2)
    lane: TLSVER
    maturity: partial
    note: NEW ROW 2026-07-28 - the TLS stack had no ledger entry at all, which is itself the finding. src/os/tls13 is 8118 lines of real TLS 1.3 - record layer, full client AND server handshake state machines, key schedule/HKDF, transcript, HelloRetryRequest, KeyUpdate, NewSessionTicket/PSK/0-RTT, extension builders, AES-128/256-GCM + ChaCha20-Poly1305, and CertificateVerify signature verify for Ed25519/RSA-PSS/ECDSA P-256/384/521. The underlying crypto is real and KAT-verified. NOT duplicated across tiers - src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/tls (63KB) is the sole TLS 1.2 impl and gc_sync_mut/gc_async_mut/nogc_async_mut are 122-1664 byte `export use` facades; nogc_async_mut_noalloc/tls is a deliberate separate baremetal client. GAPS AT HEAD - no revocation (CRL/OCSP/stapling), no KeyUsage/EKU/pathLenConstraint enforcement; the ALERT protocol is ABSENT (protocol violations drop the socket with no alert); the RFC 8446 4.1.3 downgrade sentinel is UNCHECKED; src/os/tls12 (848 lines) is message construction only. FIXED THIS LANE - RFC 6125 hostname verification was ABSENT from the entire repo (no SAN parsing, no dNSName, no wildcard matching anywhere), meaning any certificate from any trusted CA was accepted for any host; new src/os/tls13/_CertVerify/hostname_verify.spl parses subjectAltName dNSName, ASCII-folds, applies the conservative browser wildcard rule (whole leftmost label only, >=3 labels so *.com cannot match, no partial-label wildcards), ignores IP SANs, and deliberately does NOT fall back to Subject CN (RFC 6125 6.4.4) - CONVERGENCE - a parallel session then landed src/os/tls13/_CertVerify/peer_policy.spl:57 verify_peer_certificate(chain, root_store, hostname, now_unix, insecure_disable_certificate_verification) which ADOPTED this lane's function (peer_policy.spl:90 calls verify_hostname verbatim) and made peer verification UNCONDITIONAL - an empty root_store is now an explicit error rather than a bypass, the sole opt-out is config.insecure_disable_certificate_verification at one site, and _CertVerify/validity.spl adds the notBefore/notAfter check that was previously absent. So the 'default client verifies nothing' hole and the missing validity check are both CLOSED at HEAD, by that lane rather than this one. This lane deliberately did NOT restore its earlier inline call site, which would duplicate the check and partially revert the unconditional design. EVIDENCE - new spec test/03_system/os/os_tls_hostname_verify_spec.spl is 'Results: 9 total, 9 passed, 0 failed' through the real runner, and a standalone driver over the same oracles reports 36 checks / 0 failures, on real openssl-generated SAN and no-SAN certificate fixtures; 2 deliberate-red mutants (allow *.com, and no-SAN fails open) turned exactly 3 assertions red and nothing else, then reverted green. CAVEATS - the probe was run under both the default engine and SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE=interpreter with identical results, but the control used to detect an engine switch reproduces identically under both, so this is 'no divergence observed', NOT 'both engines verified'; the PRE-EXISTING TLS specs were NOT re-verified (two 600s runs produced no Results line) so no verdict is claimed for os_tls_cert_chain/client_auth/diag/hosted_interop or the 12 tls13 unit specs; and the deployed bin/simple is still the Rust SEED (it prints the seed warning), so all verdicts are seed verdicts. CERT-CHAIN SPEC RECOVERED - os_tls_cert_chain_spec.spl was 4 total / 1 passed / 3 failed at HEAD ('unsupported certificate signature algorithm'), but that is a SEED-PARSER artifact and NOT a TLS defect: the already-filed bug doc/08_tracking/bug/if_chain_last_arm_returns_previous_value_2026-07-28.md (lane IFCHAIN, src/compiler_rust/parser/src/expressions/binary.rs:68-90, Rust seed only - the pure-Simple parser is correct) glues a statement-leading '-'/'+' at the same indent onto the previous line, so the spec's `_hex_digit` helper returned 14 for 'f' and corrupted the RSA-PSS OID 2a 86 48 86 f7 0d. Replacing that helper with a table lookup - no other change to spec or source - takes it to 4 total / 4 passed / 0 failed, which clears verify_cert_chain. In the 1/4 state the lone pass was vacuous (it asserts only that a rejection occurs and got one from the corrupted-OID path, not from the BasicConstraints check it names). 24 other files carry the same helper shape including test/03_system/os/os_crypto_ref_helpers.spl and several RSA/AES/Ed25519 KAT specs, but since the defect is seed-only this does NOT undermine the KAT-verified claim; the proper fix is the parser, not 24 workarounds. src/verification/tls_isolation IS NOT TLS - it proves 4 theorems about thread-local storage (TlsStore/ThreadId/Key), builds clean with no sorry, and must not be counted as formal verification of the protocol; there is no formal TLS model in this repo. Assessment: .spipe/tls_assessment/state.md
  containers:
    owner: os container contract
    lane: A07
    maturity: partial
    note: kernel ContainerNamespaceView rootless deny-by-default enforcement + Lean-proven isolation; Podman-on-MDSOC+ manager (sys_create/pod_wire/start/stop) + OCI edge adapter landed. ENFORCED LIVE (one lookup family only) — VfsManager path ops (open/stat/readdir/mkdir/rmdir/unlink/rename/symlink/read/preload/write) now converge on enforce_lookup_grants(), which is deny-wins over the ai-cli grant AND container_view_allows_path from the kernel primitive (no second enforcement path); host context (container_view nil) short-circuits to allow, so non-container callers are byte-identical to before; a rootless/stopped container's view resolves nothing (sys_stop and the reaper already reset the view to container_view_rootless). Spec container_lookup_enforcement_spec.spl 13/13 on JIT and interpreter, 2 deliberate-red calibrations (namespace gate off -> 10 red; rootless fail-open -> exactly the 2 fail-closed rows red). STILL MODEL-ONLY: nothing binds a running task to a VfsManager view (no caller of enter_container_view outside the spec — needs a per-container VfsManager or a task-local view slot), pid lookup (pt_ext_lookup / schedctl_op_get_*) is entirely ungated, the g_vfs_* free functions in vfs_write_ops.spl bypass VfsManager and are unenforced, and nothing is armed on a boot path; QEMU/boot evidence still blocked. Plan in .spipe/container_live_wiring/state.md
  web_server:
    owner: os.http
    lane: A09
    maturity: partial
    note: native raw benchmark fast; routed server interpreter-bound
  database:
    owner: simple db embedded (SDN store)
    lane: A09
    maturity: partial
    note: SQL ITSELF IS NOT BLOCKED — Simple has its own pure-Simple SQL engine at src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/database/pure_sql/_PureDatabase/ (4,440 lines: pure_database.spl 2,973 + row_value_helpers.spl 1,467), no FFI and no sqlite dependency, so it runs in-guest where the C library cannot; exactly ONE implementation is live (the nogc_async_mut/database/pure_sql copy is a single-line re-export of the sync tier, NOT a fork, so the usual shadowed-tier trap does not apply here); it supports CREATE/DROP TABLE, CREATE/DROP INDEX (incl. UNIQUE + enforcement), ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN, INSERT (+ OR REPLACE), SELECT (WHERE, JOIN, DISTINCT, LIKE, ORDER BY, LIMIT/OFFSET, aggregates, CASE, arithmetic, scalar fns), UPDATE, DELETE, BEGIN/COMMIT/ROLLBACK, parameter binding, MVCC snapshots, a typed key API, FTS/BM25 search, and file persistence; verified 2026-07-27 at 69 examples 67 passed / 2 failed on pure_db_spec (the 2 are PRE-EXISTING and unrelated: "supports parameterized queries" hits an index-out-of-bounds, "full SQL feature integration" expects 9 to equal 2), extended spec 9/10 (1 pre-existing FTS-after-reopen failure), cache-invalidation spec 6/6; FIXED this pass — IF NOT EXISTS / IF EXISTS were parsed only for CREATE TABLE: CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS and CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS were rejected outright (the bespoke _parse_create_index text-splitter read "IF" as the index name), and DROP INDEX IF EXISTS / DROP TABLE IF EXISTS still errored on a missing object; all four now behave as SQLite does (repeat is a no-op) while bare CREATE INDEX on a duplicate name, and unknown table/column, still error, with a deliberate-red calibration confirming exactly the 3 IF-NOT-EXISTS tests flip red when the guards are disabled; NOTE this does NOT by itself unblock UiAccessStore — src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/ui/access_store.spl uses std.database.sql.connection.Database, which is an SFFI wrapper over C SQLite (std.io.sqlite_sffi), NOT pure_sql, so its CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS failure is in that shim and is fixed either by pointing UiAccessStore at PureDatabase or by fixing the shim; separately, SQLite sqlite3_vfs is no longer contract-only — src/os/port/sqlite/sqlite_vfs_impl.spl IMPLEMENTS it in pure Simple beside the declarative sqlite_vfs_contract.spl, moving real bytes through the OS file layer (35/35 spec green, plus 40 direct oracles): 14 methods REAL (xOpen xClose xRead xWrite xTruncate xSync xFileSize xDelete xAccess xFullPathname xRandomness xSleep xCurrentTime xSectorSize) — xRead zero-fills and returns the true SQLITE_IOERR_SHORT_READ, xTruncate uses the house tmp+rt_file_sync+rename pattern (the contract had listed it unsupported), xSync reaches media via rt_file_sync and SQLITE_SYNC_FULL also fsyncs the parent directory, xDelete fsyncs the parent when syncDir is set; 5 PARTIAL and honestly so (xLock/xUnlock/xCheckReservedLock reuse the ONE existing FileLock primitive, which is exclusive-only, so SHARED is over-approximated to exclusive — safe but readers serialize and RESERVED is indistinguishable from EXCLUSIVE; xFileControl handles only SIZE_HINT/HAS_MOVED and returns SQLITE_NOTFOUND otherwise; xDeviceCharacteristics returns 0 because no IOCAP bit is proven); 4 still UNSUPPORTED and FAIL CLOSED with the real SQLITE_IOERR_SHM* codes (xShmMap xShmLock xShmBarrier xShmUnmap) so WAL stays gated on the absent writable shared mmap and is NOT faked; the rollback-journal ordering (journal durable BEFORE the database page it protects is overwritten) is ENFORCED, not just documented — a page write is refused with SQLITE_IOERR while its -journal has unsynced bytes, with a crash-point test proving the pre-image is on disk before the page moves and a deliberate-red calibration proving the guard is load-bearing; the C AMALGAMATION (not SQL) is what remains blocked: sqlite3.c needs a C toolchain, so nothing is bound to it and no SQL has run through this VFS — what landed is the VFS layer the amalgamation will bind to, and its value is contingent on that binding ever happening; the durable-storage path that actually matters in-guest today runs through pure_sql + atomic.spl/FileLock, NOT through C SQLite, so the VFS is the lower-priority of the two and further VFS method work should yield to pure_sql durability — and that path has a CONFIRMED defect: PureDatabase._persist() is a plain whole-file file_write with no FileLock, no .tmp, no rt_file_sync and no rename, i.e. it does NOT use the house atomic_write pattern, so a crash mid-persist truncates the database file with no surviving previous copy (unrecoverable — fails the simple-pure-db-v1 header check on reload) and two processes on the same path interleave; pure_sql also has no on-disk journal at all (_snapshot_tables/_restore_from_snapshot are in-memory only), so a crash between COMMIT and _persist loses the transaction with no recovery record — fixing _persist to the atomic_write pattern is the highest-value durability work available on the reachable path; server tier increment 1 (sessions, capabilities, per-session write overlay, read-committed isolation) + increment 2 DURABILITY landed at src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/database/server/ — COMMIT now persists through SdnDatabase.save() (FileLock + temp + fsync + rename) BEFORE it acknowledges, all-or-nothing, crash-point matrix green at before/mid/after-persist and on a recoverable persist failure (16 examples, 3 mutants killed 12/2/1); still MODEL-ONLY: no listener (serve() drains an in-memory transport, no socket), no concurrency primitive, OPEN still trusts the claimed principal, single-row GET/PUT/DEL only, read-committed not snapshot isolation, SdnRow._version is not serialized so the optimistic check resets across a restart, and a crash after persist before ack makes the tier at-least-once (no commit ids); QUERY-CORRECTNESS pass 2026-07-28 found and FIXED five silently-wrong-result defects in the pure engine, all caught by new adversarial specs (test/02_integration/storage/dbfs/pure_db_where_semantics_spec.spl 15/15 green, was 10/15, plus pure_db_diag_spec.spl 4/4): (1) ROLLBACK restored every row as a SINGLE NULL CELL because MvccTuple.data means two different things — the typed fast INSERT path stores a positional handle "{tuple_pos}" while the slow path stores a serialized row, and _snapshot_tables captured it verbatim, so row COUNTS were right while every VALUE was destroyed and the row became unreachable by primary key (the pre-existing rollback specs asserted only rows.len(), which is exactly why this survived); (2) _restore_from_snapshot handled only 20 of the 27 per-table parallel arrays, pushing 4 without resetting them (growing to 2N per ROLLBACK) and ignoring 5 others including _tbl_typed, which is read directly at 20+ sites and never rebuilt lazily; (3) REAL literals were stored as TEXT because _is_numeric_text accepts only [-]?[0-9]+, so a column declared REAL held strings and every comparison on it was lexicographic — WHERE amount > 10 over {2.5, 30.0} returned 0 rows and WHERE amount > 10.0 returned 2; (4) _dbval_cmp/_dbval_eq took the numeric path only when BOTH sides were Integer, so mixed INTEGER/REAL compared as text (5.0 = 5 was false), which also corrupted ORDER BY, MIN/MAX and BETWEEN; (5) NULL used two-valued logic — NULL = NULL was true and NOT UNKNOWN was TRUE, so WHERE col = NULL matched the NULL rows and WHERE col != 'x' leaked them; separately the integer range fast paths compared via _dbval_as_i64, which silently reads a REAL cell as 0, and validated only the literal's type and never the column's; VERIFIED-GOOD with no change needed: AND binds tighter than OR and parentheses are honoured, CREATE INDEX is result-invariant, a UNIQUE index rejects the duplicate INSERT, and parameter binding is injection-safe (placeholders resolve to DbValue via _expr_to_dbvalue, never string-spliced); still OPEN in the engine: IN/BETWEEN bypass the new NULL guard, REAL arithmetic returns NULL and there is no division operator, LIKE is case-sensitive unlike SQLite, and _deserialize_row has one unguarded to_int() ?? 0 that reads a corrupt integer cell as 0
