    note: std.config core extracted to src/lib/common/config_core (schema+layers, mandatory-as-ceiling); IDE call-site swap pending; second non-IDE consumer = std.test_runner.test_config (TestConfig schema + workspace/session/mandatory layers, hand-rolled merge deleted)
  browser:
    owner: browser tree
    lane: A10
    maturity: model
    note: production-blocking isolation/origin/lifecycle gaps (renderer/network/GPU split multi-session). ORIGIN/COOKIE/PERMISSION MODEL IS NOW ENFORCED, not just modelled — new browsing_context.spl is the single seam: cross-document reads go through origin_policy.can_access_document (refused read yields an empty #document / empty text, never truncated content), response-body reads through can_read_response, Web Storage through storage_key/same_storage_partition (opaque origin gets key "" = no storage at all), cookies through cookie_policy.{validate_set_cookie,cookie_applies,script_visible} (HttpOnly invisible to script, Secure not attached over http:), and clipboard/navigator through PermissionSet default-deny. Ad-hoc origin comparisons DELETED at their owners — net/cors.spl cors_url_origin() + serialized-origin string equality + hand-rolled ACAO matching, CookieStore.get_header() (attached every domain/path match, ignored Secure/HttpOnly/SameSite/expiry), script_parse_url()'s silent http:// default. Evidence: test/01_unit/browser_engine/security/enforcement_spec.spl 6 blocks / 46 examples / 0 failures on JIT AND interpreter, with 4 deliberate-red mutations (can_read_response neutered, cookie_applies bypassed, partition key collapsed, can_access_document neutered) each applied ALONE, each failing 3-5 examples, each reverted. STILL BLOCKED and unchanged by this increment: renderer/network/GPU process split (no process isolation of any kind), WPT/Test262 conformance, and resource_loader.spl which has no origin to enforce on. Enforcement is in-process policy, NOT sandboxing.
